# I see mum in Russian: the -у ending
subtitle: "Say I see mum, I read a book and I drink water in Russian, and learn the -у ending that marks the thing you see, read or drink."
thumb: "band \"Look at mum. She changes.\" note \"ма́ма → ма́му\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Days of the week in Russian: сегодня, завтра","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/15-russian-days.cast"}

## I see mum in Russian: the -у ending
